  "description": "JATBOZ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C134 H106 Dy8 N10 O42. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.504-3.984 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.15-114.29°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy8(μ3-OH)6(L5)2(L6)8]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
